From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:53:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mlang: Map RFC 1766 names with MLang's own table, as Windows
 does.

Windows' MLang does not derive RFC 1766 names from the locale data.  It
enumerates a fixed table of 157 names, several of which the locale data
would not give (pt is 0816 and pt-br 0416, kz is Kyrgyz, both Serbian
locales are sr), and a name maps to the first locale that has it (es is
040a, no is 0414).

A name the table lacks but that fits in MAX_RFC1766_NAME gives the
locale of its language, the part before the first dash, with S_FALSE:
de-de is de, kok-x is kok.  Longer names are refused, except that
Rfc1766ToLcidA only looks at the first five characters.  A locale the
table lacks gets its ISO 639 language and ISO 3166 country.

MSXML takes a language argument (ms:string-compare, ms:format-date)
only when Rfc1766ToLcidW answers S_OK for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

